      "value": "The search results don't directly address the symmetry-adapted error metric. Let me verify the mathematical structure symbolically — this is the core of Hypothesis D."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "Branch 1 (correct sech) L2 relative error at t=10 will decay as a power law with N (≈N^{-2} or better depending on SSFM order), reaching below 1e-6 at N≥2048; mass drift δN/N below 1e-14, energy and momentum drift small. Branch 2 (sech²) L2 relative error will saturate at a flat plateau ≈0.17–0.18 independent of N (N=2048/4096/8192 all agree to within a few percent), confirming the structural (algebraic) floor; mass of Branch 2 will be 4/3 vs 2 for Branch 1 (relative excess −1/3), and the excess sheds into radiation visible as a dispersive background. The symbolic computation will give ε₀ = sqrt(1 + 2/3 − 2·(2/3)/2) / 1 ... concretely ε₀ = sqrt((2 + 4/3 − 2·(2/3))/2) = sqrt((10/3 − 4/3)/2) = sqrt(1) ... let me recompute carefully in the run; the predicted numeric value is ≈0.179."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
